17592186045485 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444896 1071 "![](images/55/555eec8e88dd658903e19b8779f85598f57126b054d5058b662824f09de0f6cb.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}({y}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,2]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,0]$" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444896 1072 #uuid "9b739dd6-c1ea-5425-a4f3-ff629b5d83cc" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444896 1074 "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({y}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles I and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle II covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444895 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1069 "q-80568" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1071 "![](images/12/12acb33aa174f1c174a538a89881dd19245f733c6b39df37f9ebbdc1f86442d5.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-3,1]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({2}^{x}-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1072 #uuid "fac0df1b-f9cc-511c-8006-433930d0444f" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true] [17592186444897 1074 "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/56/56f6557f98674b0f651a781e6226ba9d207273e30136e3396c3aabcf91a64024.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal ${2}^{x}-y$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({2}^{x}-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and II. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(1,0)\\in R∖D$, but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function III equals ${2}^{x}-y$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534937 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-02227aca-c031-59fd-93c4-2fafbc07e7f9" 17592186444884 "answer-264cf4e2-8ed4-58f5-90ff-ad6c657b4128" 17592186444885 "answer-6f3c18f9-58fa-5eac-9421-703a0fbb6877" 17592186444886 "answer-74756762-e410-57d4-95d6-39a30bfc37b5" 17592186444887 "answer-78cab8ed-0dae-5d25-9514-1cf1de27f303" 17592186444888 "answer-8b2af876-19a0-51e0-afde-f9a9bf4046f3" 17592186444889 "answer-8df20bc4-f189-5c1c-a2c5-e4c7ac3802cd" 17592186444890 "answer-a6c2f725-8315-5690-b52c-5a28778570c6" 17592186444891 "answer-b82083db-b8de-5a77-af8d-e0d8604e5a00" 17592186444892 "answer-dcd8a44b-f98b-5eb8-bbd1-c98d25b54697" 17592186444893 "answer-field-3c6b02fe-a198-551b-8207-64840a262a3d" 17592186444894 "answer-field-ebe09a19-f78b-5d26-9864-3cc9c0f88600" 17592186444895 "question-9b739dd6-c1ea-5425-a4f3-ff629b5d83cc" 17592186444896 "question-fac0df1b-f9cc-511c-8006-433930d0444f" 17592186444897} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
